; Stage 15 W9 item 13's second mistake class, and the one that keeps the fix
; honest. A doubled annotation desugars to a list whose head is a real type —
; `x:i32:i32` is `(i32 i32)` — so it reaches the same fall-through as
; `(nosuch i32)`. Routing every head through `unknown-type-message` would print
; "unknown type: i32 — not defined anywhere in this compilation unit", which is
; simply false, and worse than the "missing :type" message it replaced.
;
; `diagnostics.md` §"defvar" recorded the old message as acceptable; this
; fixture pins the message that names the actual mistake instead.
;
; Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "'i32' is a type, not a type constructor"
(defvar x:i32:i32 3)

(defn main ():i32
  (return 0))
